#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""llmchat: serve a Hugging Face model with vLLM on a Lambda Cloud GPU box and chat with it from this machine.

  llmchat up                 launch a box (cheapest that fits) and serve the model; reuses a running box
  llmchat ui                 Open WebUI in the browser (local, http://localhost:13000); runs `up` first if needed
  llmchat chat               terminal chat; every conversation is saved as JSON
  llmchat api [--env]        open the tunnel and print the OpenAI-compatible endpoint for scripts and eval harnesses
  llmchat status             box, model, cost so far, idle timer, tunnel and UI
  llmchat keepalive on|off   turn the box's idle auto-terminate off or back on
  llmchat logs               follow the vLLM log on the box
  llmchat ssh [cmd...]       shell on the box
  llmchat down               terminate the box and stop the tunnel and local UI
  llmchat adopt ID           manage an instance launched some other way (then run `llmchat up` to provision it)

Settings live in config.env next to this script; override them in ~/.config/lambda-llm-chat/config.env or with
LLMCHAT_<KEY>=value. The Lambda API key comes from $LAMBDA_API_KEY or ~/.config/lambda/api-key.
"""

